Z||000008||BENGAL4||03-01-2001||04:23 PM||||Chili is one of the few things I can cook. Here is my favorite recipe.<P>1-1/2 lb ground chuck<BR>1 large onion.<P>Fry beef and chopped onion together. Put into strainer and rinse fat off.<P>Add the following.<P>1 large can of whole tomatoes.<BR>2 reg cans of Brooks Chili Hot beans.<BR>1 can of diced tomatoes for chili.(cant remember brand).<BR>1 small can of tomato paste.<BR>Cover entire mixture with chili powder and cook on 1/4 impulse power for 30 min.<P>Stir and cover with chili powder again. Add 2 tablespoons of Worcestershire sauce and 10 drops of Tabasco sauce, stir and simmer for another 30 min.<P>Thats it enjoy.<P>Bill<BR>86GT 3800 II S/C<P>Cook <BR>Cover<P>||||reg||10
Z||000009||loafer87gt||03-01-2001||05:34 PM||||mmmm, Sloppy Joes!||||reg||1
Z||000010||Cliff Pennock||03-01-2001||05:55 PM||||1 lb ground beef<BR>1-2 large onions<BR>1 can of beans<BR>2 tomatoes<BR>mushrooms<BR>chili powder, salt, pepper, sugar.<P>Fry onions with salt and pepper until brown. add ground beef and fry until brown. Add mushrooms and (cut up) tomatoes. Add chili powder. Let it simmer and at the end, add one tea-spoon of sugar. Eat. Wait 30 minutes and run for the toilet! Also, don't eat near open fires.||||reg||1
